Quoting  jerk-o  <jerk-o@yomomma.org>:
[Multiplayer multi-character NH]

Personally, I think this is a complete nonstarter. Notwithstanding the
agonising definitions pedantry in the other subthread, hotseating's
clearly impractical for a game as big as NH, the ability to think is a
basic part of what the game is, etc. It could be done but it wouldn't be a
good game. That said;

>Some other "balance issues" I was thinking of:
>Escaping to the planes
>Offering the amulet

We discussed this in some depth at London rgrn. I'd do the following with
the invocation artifacts and the amulet;

If one of these artifacts has been removed from its resting place, going
there gets you a thingy that tells you what level it's on.
If no character who's ever seen a given item is alive and its normal
starting level is empty, that level is reset and the item returned to its
starting place. (More generally, levels could be reset when no-one alive
has seen them).
In the Planes, you can never advance further into the Planes than the
Amulet. The Planes count as one level for the purposes of the last
mechanism, so as long as someone's on any Plane the Amulet stays there; if
everyone dies on the Planes, the Amulet goes back to the Sanctum.
Without PvP, everyone in the invocation room ascends. If there is PvP,
you'd want some explicit alliance mechanism - or just say only one person
can ascend to give a motive for an endgame fight (at the very least, only
people of the right alignment can ascend).

>Having more than one of the same class on the quest (Who gets the quest
>reward)

I would make quests individually instantiated; tackle your quest alone. If
your quest artifact's already out there, you get an item like the ones
described for the invocation artifacts, but which grants some subset of
the powers of the real one. "Shadow of the Orb of Fate", or whatever.
Again, if no-one's ever seen the real one, the next person to do the Quest
gets it.

>Wishing for the quest reward of another class when they're in the game

I wouldn't let any character use another class's Quest artifact under ay
circumstances.

>Can new characters join the game that's been in progress for a while?

Yes, but their starting equipment should be "stuck" to them for some
number of turns - if they drop it, other people can't see it, and if they
die, it evaporates. Otherwise everyone would sacrifice L1 wizards on the
altar of getting a CoMR. The level reset mechanism would never reset DL 1
(unless everyone died) but lower levels would often be reset if the heroes
suffered a serious setback.
